Z||000000||saleenfiero||07-06-2001||02:17 PM||||I was cruising around town, just for fun.  Stereo going loud, windows down.  I then pull up to a red light and a brand new Denali Yukon pulls up beside me.  There's a kid in the passenger seat eyeing up my car so I decide I will show this overfed SUV what I got.  Turns green, I stomp on it.  So does the Denali.  He keeps up - easily.  It was when he proceeded to really get into it and blow by me that I saw the "supercharged" decal on the ass end.<BR>Oh well, I felt better later, I pull up next to a yellow hayabusa bike.  One of those times, if you're too dumb to race, you deserve to get smoked.  He revs the absolute crap out of the bike and I look over like he's retarded.  Light turns green, I don't stomp on it, just go normal.  And I look back, HE STALLED IT.  Heh, so I mat the accellerator, knowing he could still easily blow by me.  He stalls 3 times before he gets going and I am in the next turning lane up ahead.  Just between you and me, let's just call it a win.<BR>Kinda reminds me of the time my friend and I were driving along in his POS '81 mustang with the lowly 3.3 inline 6.  A brand new Camaro SS rolls up next to us.  I'm already counting the car lengths ahead and how many he will win by.  I'm thinking 50 car lengths or so.  Light goes green.  My friend mats it and the Camaro does.  To bad the Camaro was in reverse as the time, so he smokes the tires backwards and then stalls.  Oh well.||||reg||2
Z||000001||FieroJoe||07-06-2001||02:23 PM||||How the heck does someone put their car into reverse when they are going to race?<P>I just don't understand how that can be possible!  Must have scared the hell out of the person stopped behind him though!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||p4n1c||07-06-2001||02:28 PM||||That first thing is like a bunch of retards in a QX4 thinking they could beat my friends beat up old GMC Sierra pickup with a 305.<P>They had come flying out of a gas station and almost rolled it, then they started squeeling in reverse and forward at a red light.  Light turns green and my friend comes a little faster then normal(didn't floor it) and we put about 3 - 4 car lengths between them and us by the next light.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4<BR>*Under Restoration*||||reg||1
