Z||000004||mrgone||07-06-2001||04:31 PM||||maybe was a 4 speed, and thought R was 1st<P>i dont know if ss's are 4 speed. i think their 6... so lessee...  yeah the r would be the same as 1st on a 6.<P>and if it was new he prolly wasnt used to it.<BR>not that im sticking up for him. still a stupid move<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||07-06-2001||04:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroJoe:<BR><B>How the heck does someone put their car into reverse when they are going to race?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well I did it at a stop sign the day I bought my fiero and was bringing it home.  You see I am use to driving a 5 speed so it is kinda instinctive to move the shift to the left and up (which is 1st gear in a 5 speed but reverse in a fiero 4 speed).  I revved the engine to 3 grand an popped the clutch.  Next thing I know my head almost hits the steering wheel.  Talk about embarrassing.  Thank God no one was behind me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||07-06-2001||06:10 PM||||I did it with my '69 Camaro, the worst part is that it was on the dragstip with everybody watching. I had just taken the four speed out (blew it up) and put the stock three speed back in. Boy did I feel like an ass!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||11
